   "source": [
    "Bonus Exercise 7\n",
    "Marketing Channel vs Customer Response\n",
    "\n",
    "The assignment specifically suggests using melt()."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "af83768a-6518-4b77-b3b7-7898b2b646ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "Step 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Create response indicator\n",
    "\n",
    "marketing_df[\"response_yes\"] = (\n",
    "    marketing_df[\"response\"] == \"Yes\"\n",
    ").astype(int)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5aa0396e-e895-41aa-9d70-0966a471a466",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "Step 2\n",
    "\n",
    "Select the required columns\n",
    "\n",
    "channels = marketing[\n",
    "    [\"sales_channel\", \"response_yes\"]\n",
    "]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2d3cb7f8-77d6-4439-8948-bce600b8f476",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "Step 3\n",
    "\n",
    "Use melt()\n",
    "\n",
    "long_channels = channels.melt(\n",
    "    id_vars=\"sales_channel\",\n",
    "    value_vars=[\"response_yes\"],\n",
    "    var_name=\"response_type\",\n",
    "    value_name=\"response\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "long_channels.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c181d6de-215d-47de-857d-6552a19bf145",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "Step 4\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate response rate\n",
    "\n",
    "response_rate = (\n",
    "    long_channels\n",
    "    .groupby(\"sales_channel\")[\"response\"]\n",
    "    .mean()\n",
    "    .mul(100)\n",
    "    .round(2)\n",
    "    .reset_index()\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "response_rate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7112ec4d-26e0-4de2-8d09-2b3c4929f648",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Final Markdown Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "The response rate measures the percentage of customers who responded positively to the marketing campaign for each sales channel. Comparing these rates helps identify the most effective marketing channels. Channels with higher response rates are likely more successful at engaging customers and should be considered for future marketing investments."
   ]
  },
